// Sentinel tests — pinned to the codegen limitations the Never-type PR
// shipped with. Each test asserts that the *currently-broken* position
// FAILS to compile today (`expect_failure = true`).
//
// When a future PR extends `is_iife_eligible_rvalue` /
// `generate_expr_into_local` (or otherwise lifts diverging sub-exprs out
// of these positions), one of these tests will start compiling
// successfully — which causes `expect_failure = true` to mark it as a
// test failure, forcing the author of the fix to flip the assertion in
// the same commit.
//
// Flip pattern when fixed:
//   - Replace `@test(expect_failure = true)` with `@test(output = "<expected>")`.
//     to drop the now-supported position.
//
// Each sentinel is in its own file so positions can be flipped
// independently as their codegen path lands.
//
// FLIPPED: array-literal, tuple, index, function-call-arg positions all
// work end-to-end now. The hoist arms in `generate_expr_into_local` cover
// these shapes; tail-position fncalls (`fn f() { print(if c { 42 } else
// { return }) }`) are routed via the statement path in
// `generate_ast_function_body`. Runtime tests live in
// `tests/never_type_test.rock`. This file is currently empty of sentinels
// — the next still-broken position to be discovered should be added here.
